## DESCRIPTION
## Find percentages of tint in colored paints.
## ENDDESCRIPTION
## DBsubject(Arithmetic)
## DBchapter(Percents)
## DBsection(Applications)
## KEYWORDS('percent', 'tint', 'paint')
## Level(5)
## MO(1)

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Numeric");
$a            = random(30, 60, 10);
$b            = random(5,  10, 1);
$lityellow    = $a * 0.3;
$newlityellow = $lityellow + $b;
$newtotal     = $a + $b;
$z            = 1000 * $newlityellow;
$x            = $z % $newtotal;
$y            = ($x >= .5 * $newtotal) ? .1 : 0;
$ans          = ($z - $x) / ($newtotal * 10) + $y;
$unrounded    = 100 * $newlityellow / $newtotal;
BEGIN_PGML
A mixture of [$a] liters of paint is 25% red tint, 30% yellow tint and 45% water. Five ([$b]) liters of yellow tint are added to the original mixture.

The percent of yellow tint in the new mixture is [_]{$ans}

Answer must be correct to 1 decimal place.
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_HINT
Hint: You need to find the amount of yellow tint in the new mixture and the number of liters of new mixture.

END_PGML_HINT

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
In the original mixture there was [`0.30\times [$a]=[$lityellow]`] liters of yellow tint.

In the new mixture there is [`[$lityellow]+[$b]=[$newlityellow]`] liters of
yellow.

The number of liters of the new mixture is [`[$a]+[$b]=[$newtotal]`].  
Thus, the answer  (before rounding) is [`100\times \frac{[$newlityellow]}{[$newtotal]}=[$unrounded]`]%.
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
